        },
        "message": "modemfwd: Suppress EX_USAGE error for unsupported power_on/power_off\n\nNot all modem helpers support the --power_on and --power_off flags (for\nexample, rolling-helper exits with EX_USAGE (64) during flag parsing).\nAdditionally, Daemon::ChangeModemPowerState unconditionally invoked\nhelper->PowerOn() whenever Shill's Powered property changed to true,\neven when the modem was already in PowerState::ON or PowerState::LOW.\n\n1. In RunHelperProcess, log at EVLOG(1) instead of LOG(ERROR) when\n   power_on or power_off exits with EX_USAGE (64).\n2. In Daemon::ChangeModemPowerState, only call helper->PowerOn() when\n   the current modem power state is OFF or UNKNOWN.\n3. Default-initialize state_ and power_state_ to UNKNOWN in ModemImpl\n   and StubModem.\n\nBUG=b:532221786\nTEST=cros_run_unit_tests --board=nissa --packages chromeos-base/modemfwd\n\nChange-Id: I7abf6f8a61f36f42363106a6664076e23ac6e8bf\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform2/+/8750359\nCommit-Queue: Rukun Mao <rmao@google.com>\nTested-by: Rukun Mao <rmao@google.com>\nReviewed-by: Daniel Winkler <danielwinkler@google.com>\n",
