        "committer": {
          "name": "Chromium LUCI CQ",
          "email": "chromium-scoped@luci-project-accounts.iam.gserviceaccount.com",
          "time": "Sun Nov 08 23:16:26 2026"
        },
        "message": "Open download intermediate URIs with an explicit read/write mode\n\nDownloadDocumentUriBridge::OpenDocumentUri() opened the intermediate\ndocument with FLAG_OPEN_ALWAYS | FLAG_WRITE | FLAG_READ. The document\nalready exists because DownloadCollectionBridge created it, so the\ncreate-if-absent part of OPEN_ALWAYS was never needed; the Android\nadapter mapped the combination to \"rw\". A later CL in this series\nrejects OPEN_ALWAYS for content URIs, since Android providers cannot\nhonor create-or-open by name, which would make every download to a\ndocument URI fail at BaseFile initialization.\n\nOpen the URI with base::OpenAndroidDocument() and\nAndroidDocumentAccessMode::kReadWrite. This asks the provider for\nexactly the mode the download already used: read access so BaseFile can\nhash the bytes of a resumed download, and no truncation.\n\nBug: 543633476\nChange-Id: Id88f93c3168f6809c6bfdac96d5e00fa4ae7241f\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8461822\nReviewed-by: Shuhei Takahashi <nya@chromium.org>\nCommit-Queue: Keigo Oka <oka@chromium.org>\nReviewed-by: Min Qin <qinmin@chromium.org>\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1738696}\n",
        "tree_diff": [
